    "explanation": "The rider's claim and the platform's own trace agree, so this dispute is decided on the numbers.\n\n(1) The deviation is ESTABLISHED. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02830 measures the trip between the recorded pickup and drop-off events at 22.95 km against the booked optimal of 16.7 km on EV-TRIP-02830 — an excess of 6.25 km, which is 37.43% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km). The trace distance governs; the rounded 22.9 km convenience copy on the trip record was not used for the threshold.\n\n(2) The trace is not impaired. 181 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s, so none of POL-RD-07(a)–(c) fires. No independent corroboration is required, and the POL-RD-08 burden shifts to the driver.\n\n(3) The driver's traffic excuse does not answer the finding. You say there was a massive jam on the expressway. An external-traffic excuse is tested under POL-RD-03 against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else. The only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02830-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT): it names no road, carries no validity window and holds no shortest-lawful-alternative figure. POL-RD-03 cannot be run and, under POL-RD-13 read with POL-RD-08, the assertion carries no weight — it neither reduces the excess nor supplies an amended optimal. Because you named no evidence ID for an advisory, POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged (POL-RD-13(1)): this is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it. The ruling records that the assertion was discarded and that no advisory was on file.\n\n(4) The arithmetic. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs; the surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 16.7 + 0.28 × 22.5) × 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 23.425. Charged_total is 30.18. Refund = 30.18 − 23.425 = 6.755, rounded UP to SGD 6.80. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90% full